%erg 0.1
Title: Capture full usage dict (reasoning_tokens) in query_single_turn
Created: 2026-05-21
Author: claude

--- log ---
2026-05-21T10:00Z claude created — probe confirmed OpenRouter passes reasoning_tokens; harness strips them

--- body ---
## Context

`harness.py:492-495` constructs a stripped-down `usage` dict containing
only `prompt_tokens` and `completion_tokens`, discarding the rest of the
`response.usage` object — including `completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens`.

A 10-call probe (2026-05-21) against OpenRouter confirmed:
- OpenRouter reliably populates `completion_tokens_details.reasoning_tokens`
  for both reasoning models (gpt-oss-*, qwen3-max-thinking, deepseek-v4-pro)
  and non-reasoning baselines (where the value is 0).
- Our `worker.py:347` stores whatever `usage` dict `query_single_turn`
  returns, so the data is lost at the harness boundary, not at the worker.

Consequence: Exp 1 raw JSONs cannot tell us whether thinking-capable models
actually reasoned. Annex A "Reasoning" column is based on registry
metadata, not measurement.

## Fix

In `query_single_turn`, replace the hand-built two-key dict with
`response.usage.model_dump()` (OpenAI SDK Pydantic model → dict).
This preserves `completion_tokens_details`, `prompt_tokens_details`,
and any future fields the SDK exposes.

## Test

Mock a response with `completion_tokens_details = {"reasoning_tokens": 42}`
and assert it survives in the returned `usage` dict.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `query_single_turn` returns the full usage dict.
- [ ] New regression test in `tests/test_harness.py` pins the contract.
- [ ] Existing tests still pass.
- [ ] Worker raw JSON downstream is unchanged (still writes `usage` as-is).

## Out of scope

- Surfacing `reasoning_tokens` in `records_to_metrics()` / Annex A column —
  separate ticket. This one is the capture-side fix; the analysis side
  is a downstream consumer change.
- Registry-level redesign (per-row reasoning_effort grids) — separate
  design dialogue.
